# Template for dubplate-server's own /etc/dubplate/env, rendered by
# scripts/deploy.sh from this file plus the sourced workstation age-store
# values (~/.local/secrets), exactly as env/dubplate.env.template renders
# for the incumbent. internal/config is dubplate-server's own wall
# (config.go, keys.go); this file is its render manifest, not the wall
# itself.
#
# Three row states, so a later rung does not re-derive them
# (spec:1339-1348):
#   - A bare NAME= line resolves from the workstation age store at render
#     time, or deploy.sh aborts, listing every name it could not resolve.
#   - A NAME=value line is a literal: a value that will never be minted,
#     because it is not a secret.
#   - A commented-out NAME= line (none below yet) is a name whose value
#     arrives later, on the config.WallRow.Pending precedent: a row the
#     wall owns but does not require yet.
#
# No row here is a secret, so no name in this file is minted via
# secret-set.sh and none is added to ~/.dotfiles/secrets/registry.md.
# CLAUDE.md's "adding a name there requires minting it" rule reads against
# the incumbent manifest, whose every row is a store lookup; the rename
# below (DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_DIR to DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT,
# DUBPLATE_SERVE_SITE_NAME to DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME) is why this file's rows
# ship as literals instead: the age store still carries the old names, and
# a bare row here would look them up under the new name and abort.

# Owned wall (config.go:216, keys.go's ownedWall): every row below is
# required by internal/config.Load with no default.

# DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT exists only to satisfy config.Load's wall
# (config.go:216); nothing in internal/engine/shadow reads it
# (grep-confirmed). It is a literal, not a bare row, because the age
# store carries the pre-rename name DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_DIR
# (internal/config/keys.go:165-166), and a bare DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT=
# row here would resolve against a name the store does not have.
DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT=/srv/music/library

# DUBPLATE_STATE_DIR is /var/lib/dubplate, deliberately not the
# incumbent's /var/lib/musicbox: a shared directory would grant the
# shadow unit write access over the incumbent's lock file, tag logs, and
# run reports, which is exactly the grant the read-only guarantee exists
# to withhold (spec:1226-1237). It is a literal, not a bare row, for a
# different reason than the rename above: DUBPLATE_STATE_DIR is already
# exported into deploy.sh's one flat shell namespace, carrying the
# incumbent's value. The mechanism, precisely: the incumbent template's
# own bare DUBPLATE_STATE_DIR= row (env/dubplate.env.template) forces the
# name into ~/.local/secrets, deploy.sh:93-96 sources that file before
# this file's render runs, and a bare row here would resolve via
# deploy.sh:182's indirect expansion against that same shell variable,
# silently inheriting /var/lib/musicbox. The render loop itself exports
# nothing; it appends to an array. A literal here is the only way to give
# dubplate-server its own value.
DUBPLATE_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/dubplate

# DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME is a literal for the same rename reason as
# DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT above: the age store carries the pre-rename name
# DUBPLATE_SERVE_SITE_NAME (internal/config/keys.go:165-166). Its value is
# copied verbatim from the store's DUBPLATE_SERVE_SITE_NAME (Resolution
# R7), never invented; see docs/HISTORY.md's Task 2 entry for the copy's
# provenance, not this comment.
DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME=907

# DUBPLATE_ADMIN_EMAIL is already minted under this exact name (no
# rename), so it stays a bare row: deploy.sh resolves it from the age
# store at render time.
DUBPLATE_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# Shadow integration (keys.go's integrationClasses, "shadow", rung 4):
# adopter-optional, read-only observation of the incumbent's import
# pipeline. All six rows ship together; an adopter who does not run the
# incumbent sets the flag to an explicit false and removes the other
# five (config_test.go:307-310).
#
# DUBPLATE_SHADOW_ENABLED=true is load-bearing in a way the rows below
# it are not: with the flag false or absent, cfg.Shadow stays nil and
# shadow observe refuses, naming the flag. A Required or Optional row
# set beside a false or absent flag is a load error naming the flag
# (config.go:190-192).
DUBPLATE_SHADOW_ENABLED=true

# The three path rows below are required-when-enabled
# (keys.go's shadow class, Required).

# DUBPLATE_SHADOW_OBSERVE_DIR is the inbox the incumbent consumes.
DUBPLATE_SHADOW_OBSERVE_DIR=/srv/music/inbox

# DUBPLATE_SHADOW_ORACLE_STATE_DIR is where the incumbent's
# report-*.json and import-*.log live.
DUBPLATE_SHADOW_ORACLE_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/musicbox

# DUBPLATE_SHADOW_REVIEW_DIR is where a skipped album is filed.
DUBPLATE_SHADOW_REVIEW_DIR=/srv/music/review

# The floor and the budget below are Optional (keys.go's shadow class):
# accepted as registered thresholds with a default, never required.
# Both ship as literals matching thresholds.go's registered defaults
# exactly (Resolution R8), so the value here and the default in code
# agree by inspection rather than by trusting an unset row.

# DUBPLATE_SHADOW_FLOOR duplicates thresholds.go's registered default
# for the shadow floor (Resolution R8).
DUBPLATE_SHADOW_FLOOR=720h

# DUBPLATE_SHADOW_BUDGET duplicates thresholds.go's registered default
# for the shadow request budget (Resolution R8).
DUBPLATE_SHADOW_BUDGET=60
